                           "predicate":  "is_constrained_by",
                           "value":  "3GPP MC service layer boundary",
                           "unit":  null,
                           "author":  "amina",
                           "role":  "mcx-service-architect",
                           "confidence":  "designed",
                           "verbatim":  "The MCX layer delivers group voice, data and video to dispatchers and field teams, and it has to keep delivering group voice when almost nothing else works. Our boundary is the 3GPP MC service layer: group and affiliation management, floor control, media distribution, and the interworking function towards the legacy LMR fleet, which stays for four more years. Everything below - bearers, QoS, slices - belongs to the core team.  What must survive is talkgroup communication inside an isolated site: if the transport to the national data centres is cut, a site must keep serving its local talkgroups. That is a hard requirement from the customer, and I do not yet know whether the platform we shortlist can do it without a local instance.",
